{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeEs37NJrJbgwgSMhcamW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The driver commits on the iteration's behalf from a prepared message file. Writing it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":693,"cache_read_input_tokens":209584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":693},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da811920-c880-42ff-a202-5749e1a7ccdc","uuid":"d30245b3-9701-4b57-a658-de7169e52317","timestamp":"2026-08-20T23:24:52.524Z","request_id":"req_011CeEs36B8U3o151M93E7V5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeEs37NJrJbgwgSMhcamW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013LkQChVnVUZMuJ83zBGkiG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p11.txt <<'EOS'\n1.11: deferring the ATTN_SPLIT join past i:qidx and i:iw is worth -0.542 +/- 0.310 ms/forward drift-free and -1.092 +/- 0.146 at ctx 12,410 -- and ONE arm order called it a null\n\nWHAT CHANGED. kernels/compressed_decode.cu. compressed_verify_step_indexer forks the two\ncompressor_emit_group calls onto g_side and joined them straight back, immediately after build_qKV.\nNothing between there and index_score reads what the emits write: the first consumer of idx_ckv is\nindex_score and of comp_kv is the kv_all copy, while i:qidx (a GEMM on iqrq/iqrs) and i:iw (a GEMM\non x_cur) read neither. The cudaEventRecord stays where the emits end; only the cudaStreamWaitEvent\nmoves, down to index_score. NO_JOIN_DEFER=1 restores the 1.8 position on the same binary, which is\nwhat let both arms be one build. ADOPTED, DEFAULT ON.\n\nWHAT WAS MEASURED. Drift-free paired over 18 legs and FOUR checkpoint loads:\n-0.542 +/- 0.310 ms/forward, and -1.092 +/- 0.146 at ctx 12,410 where it is 6/6 in each arm order\nindependently (+0.77 % tok/s). The marks show the mechanism at K=5: cattn:compress 2.34 -> 0.07 ms\nas the barrier leaves it, i:qidx 1.94 -> 2.81 as it ABSORBS the emit traffic -- the same signature\nFinding 56 recorded -- verify TOTAL 127.33 -> 125.89. -1.44 ms on an emit step x 1.8's 64.9 % emit\nrate predicts -0.93 ms/forward.\n\nWHAT IT MEANS, AND IT IS NOT THE 0.54. Run the standard way -- control arm first, so drift penalises\nthe change -- this measured -0.324, 2 SE [-0.670, +0.022]: a band covering zero, which under the\nitem's own pre-registration is a NEGATIVE RESULT and would have been written up as one. It is not\none. Pairing removes between-LEG variance and does nothing to a constant offset between two\ncheckpoint loads, and traps SS19 had already measured that offset at 0.6 % = ~0.8 ms/forward -- the\nsize of the entire effect. Running the identical pair with the ARM ORDER REVERSED gives\n-0.760 [-1.109, -0.411]; averaging the per-leg deltas cancels the drift and half their difference\nmeasures it: THE SECOND CHECKPOINT LOAD OF A SESSION COSTS +0.218 +/- 0.157 ms/forward, 40 % of what\nthis item was chasing. Term A needs another 22.4 ms and there is no single 22 ms item left, so it\nwill be paid down in pieces this size. Below ~1 ms/forward, a null from one arm order is not a\nresult, and reporting one retires a real win. tools/paired_band.py --reversed does the pooling.\n\na AND b ARE UNCHANGED AT 125.11 AND 1.887, ON PURPOSE. The item pre-registered a FLAT saving --\nevery byte in the deferred window is context-independent, and the mark-level confirmation was taken\nat context FIVE. The engine did not deliver a flat one: -1.092 +/- 0.146 at ctx 12,410 (sd 0.179)\nagainst bands covering zero at 3,197 and 6,260 (sd 0.585, 0.741). A three-point fit through groups\nwith 3-4x different scatter is not an attribution, so the ratchet is stated where it resolves --\na + b*ctx at ctx 12,410 goes 142.24 -> 141.15 ms -- and the term is new item 1.13. The item says its\nown prediction failed rather than rounding it into the nearest term.\n\nBIT-EXACT, AND THE GATE FOR IT DID NOT EXIST. tests/gate_join_defer.cu is the FIRST gate in this\nrepo that calls arena_init() before driving these kernels. Every other one links them without an\narena, so g_side is null, asplit is false, and the fork 1.8 priced at 0.81 ms/forward had never been\nunder test at all. It refuses to PASS if g_side comes back null. Four cases (1 emit, 2 emits, 0\nemits, a second shape), both join positions in one process on identical weights: 0 of 143,360 floats\ndiffer, same under --swap, and --negctl fires on every case so the memcmp is live. Engine: identical\ngenerated ids in both arms, LOSSLESS PASS in both, 44 of 44 sweep legs byte-identical with tau equal\nto three decimals across four loads.\n\nTHE GATE'S FIRST RUN SAID FAIL, AND THE NULL CONTROL IS WHY THAT IS NOT A DEFECT IN THIS COMMIT.\nOne row differed -- row 0, an M=1 decode step, which 1.11 does not touch. Pinning BOTH arms to the\nSAME join position still differed, including with the pre-1.11 code in both; duplicating a case\nshowed instance 1 differing and instance 2 of byte-identical data clean. It is being FIRST: the\narena slab is cudaMalloc'd and never zeroed, so scratch in the M=1 step is read before it is written\nand sees driver garbage on pass 1 and the previous pass's bytes forever after. Pre-existing,\nunrelated, burned off with a discarded warm arm, and filed as new ladder item 1.14 -- it has been\nsilently corrupting the first run of every bit-exactness gate here.\n\nWIKI, in the same commit: kernel-optimisations.md SS2.10 (the adopted win; the general form is that\na join position is a free parameter and the default is the wrong one),\nmeasurement-and-traps.md SS32 (the cold-arena first pass) and SS33 (pairing does not remove a\nbetween-load offset), context-scaling.md (the flat/context attribution left open and why), and\nREADME.md's state table.\n\nDetached: scripts/joindefer_ab_run.sh, 8 phases, both arm orders, named in detach_audit.sh's\nPATTERNS in this commit.\nEOS\nwc -l evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p11.txt","description":"Write the prepared commit message"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":693,"cache_read_input_tokens":209584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":693},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da811920-c880-42ff-a202-5749e1a7ccdc","uuid":"2279c7f9-29e7-48f6-9b32-70c25f42c528","timestamp":"2026-08-20T23:25:19.662Z","request_id":"req_011CeEs36B8U3o151M93E7V5"}
