{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeEs7YodMeF281xKw7PPZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration 8 done — ladder item **1.11**, one item, a kernel change, adopted.\n\n## What shipped\n\n`kernels/compressed_decode.cu`: `compressed_verify_step_indexer` forked the compressor emits onto `g_side` and joined them back immediately after `build_qKV`. Nothing between there and `index_score` reads what the emits write, so the `cudaEventRecord` stays put and only the `cudaStreamWaitEvent` moves down to the true dependency. `NO_JOIN_DEFER=1` restores the old position on the same binary. Default ON.\n\n## What it measures\n\nDrift-free paired over 18 legs and **four** checkpoint loads: **−0.542 ± 0.310 ms/forward**, and **−1.092 ± 0.146 at ctx 12,410** (6/6 in each arm order independently, +0.77 % tok/s). Marks confirm the mechanism at K=5: `cattn:compress` 2.34 → 0.07 ms as the barrier leaves it, `i:qidx` 1.94 → 2.81 as it absorbs the traffic, verify TOTAL 127.33 → 125.89.\n\n**The headline is the method, not the 0.54.** Run the standard way — control arm first — it measured **−0.324, 2 SE [−0.670, +0.022]**, a band covering zero, which under the item's own pre-registration is a negative result. Pairing removes between-leg variance and does nothing to a between-*load* offset, which traps §19 already put at ~0.8 ms/forward — the size of the whole effect. Reversing the arm order and pooling cancels it and measures it: **the second checkpoint load of a session costs +0.218 ± 0.157 ms/forward.** Below ~1 ms/forward, a null from one arm order is not a result.\n\n## What I did not claim\n\n`a` and `b` stay at 125.11 and 1.887. The item pre-registered a **flat** saving; the engine gave one that resolves only at ctx 12,410 and covers zero at 3,197 and 6,260, and a three-point fit through groups with 3–4× different scatter is not an attribution. The ratchet is stated where it resolves (142.24 → 141.15 ms at ctx 12,410) and the term is new item 1.13.\n\n## Bit-exactness\n\n`tests/gate_join_defer.cu` is the first gate here that calls `arena_init()` first — every other gate links these kernels without an arena, so `g_side` is null and the fork 1.8 priced at 0.81 ms/forward had never been under test. 0 of 143,360 floats differ, same under `--swap`, `--negctl` fires. 44/44 sweep legs byte-identical, `tau` equal to three decimals, LOSSLESS PASS both arms.\n\nIts first run said FAIL on one row — an M=1 decode step 1.11 doesn't touch. The null control (both arms pinned to the same join position, including pre-1.11 code in both) still differed, and a duplicated case showed instance 1 differing and instance 2 clean: the arena slab is never zeroed and the first pass reads scratch it never wrote. Pre-existing, filed as item 1.14, and it has been silently corrupting the first run of every bit-exactness gate in this repo.\n\nWiki updated in the same iteration: `kernel-optimisations.md` §2.10, `measurement-and-traps.md` §32/§33, `context-scaling.md`, and README's state table. `scripts/joindefer_ab_run.sh` is in `detach_audit.sh`'s patterns.\n\n**One thing to note:** `git add`/`commit`/`push` are denied by `.claude/settings.json`, so I could not commit or push. I left the prepared message at `evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p11.txt`, which is the convention `scripts/decode_loop.sh` reads — the driver will commit and push on the iteration's behalf. If you're running this outside the driver, that file is the message."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":442,"cache_read_input_tokens":213426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":442},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da811920-c880-42ff-a202-5749e1a7ccdc","uuid":"a895d2f0-3ef4-42ad-af2a-b1e68c81d384","timestamp":"2026-08-20T23:26:09.622Z","request_id":"req_011CeEs7XKLAHLLss767qEUx"}
